Z||000010||Pontiaddict||10-26-2000||08:04 PM||||If they make it big enough to put a LS1 sideways in the back. The rest of the problems would take care of themselves.||||reg||1
Z||000011||87ECO5||10-27-2000||06:31 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Jaei Sun:<BR><B>Now imagine some Pontiac styling added to it.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That's what scares me!  Other than a few Pegasus emblems and MAYBE a "FORMULA" decal on each door, this car should be left alone!<P>Pontiac will get a hold of it and destroy it!  The car is clean as is.  The last thing it needs is tacked-on ribbed body cladding and badging for everything from "ABS" and "EFI" to "RAM AIR" and "2.2 LITER OHC"!<P>I agree that it's a diamond in the rough.  Give us a few amenities and good crash protection, slap a "Fiero" emblem on the back and sell it for $20,000 (MR2 and Miata territory)!<P>If Pontiac builds it, they will come!||||reg||1
Z||000012||Tigger||10-27-2000||08:48 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by webbee:<BR><B>Isn't Opel a Ford product?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Nope it's GM, but Opel could have been apart of Ford at one time.<P>For some nonsense auto trivia...  The Cadillac Catera is based on the Opel Omega, and the new Saturn LS is based from the Opel Vectra.<P><P>------------------<BR>T-T-F-N, Tah Tah For Now!<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tiggerblue.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000013||william_thorniii||10-27-2000||10:22 AM||||Patrick's Dad,<P>"Personally, I'd like to see the Cadillac Catera with the LS1 and B/W 6-speed, as outfitted by Opel in Europe. Caddy thinks that they'd only sell "a thousand or so." Duh."... GM sells that exact car in Australia...except I think it comes with a 5 speed.  Check out Holden's web site if you want to look at some jaw-dropping "family sedans"<P>87EC05,<P>That is EXACTLY why I want to move to Europe... Americans have no sense of refinement and can not recognize a good design when they have one on the moniter in front of them.  The Catera is the worst "refreshing" I have ever seen of the Opel, Holden or whatever it was first.   Aren't we lucky?<P>William T. Thorn, III<BR>||||reg||14
Z||000014||bHooper||10-27-2000||10:41 AM||||Opel has been a part of GM for years... remember the old Opel GT?  That was sold through Buick dealers in the early 70's.<P>I will definately buy one of these cars, if they bring it over, and if they dont add 1500 lbs to it!<P>Price, doesnt matter when it comes to being happy!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT||||reg||1
Z||000015||yobtah||10-27-2000||12:17 PM||||Also from the Car and Driver article:<P>"Now for the big question:  Will the Speedster come to America, perhaps as a resurrected Fiero?  Let us answer that succinctly:  Is crack cocaine a healthy way to lose weight?"<P>"...and the Speedster's build quality is suspect:  Our car's cable shifter misplaced two gears, its lone wiper blade ejected not far from an enormous stork's nest, its defroster required assistance from two men with Handi Wipes, and the cockpit-borne rattles had, by day's end, become their own hip-hop band."<P>"There's an outfit in Opel's hometown of Russelsheim that serves deep-fried calves' brains.  That this product is popular in Germany in no way guarantees its success in America.  If you don't believe us, ask your dad what he recalls of the Opel GT."<P>I'd say its chances of coming to the US are very slim.  I'm also not sure we'd want it if it did.||||reg||1
Z||000016||Pontiaddict||10-27-2000||09:00 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 87ECO5:<BR><B>Pontiac will get a hold of it and destroy it!  The car is clean as is.  The last thing it needs is tacked-on ribbed body cladding and badging for everything from "ABS" and "EFI" to "RAM AIR" and "2.2 LITER OHC"!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You mean Like they destroyed GM's best selling car, the Grand AM? If you took all of the ribs off of the body, and took the badges off, you would get a Malibu! As far as I can tell, everybody thinks the Malibu is ugly and looks like a Camry. Everybody thinks that a Camaro looks like a Chrysler Sebring even though the Camaro was the car that had it's styling ripped off. Nobody Mistakes the styling of a Trans Am. The only thing Pontiac has control of on their cars, is the styling. They look outrageous beacuse they can get away with doing it. The reason they made the Aztek look like it does, is because if they didn't, GM would have spread whatever bland styling the Aztec would have recieved to the rest of Pontiac's lineup. <P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by JohnnyK:<BR><B>We all love the Fiero, but you guys actually like Pontiac?? Actually think they are a good car company?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>If the Fiero wasn't made by Pontiac, I'd probably never have bought one. Who do you think should have built it, Oldsmobile?||||reg||1
